  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 145 PM CDT Wed Sep 23 2026\n\nCurrent Conditions and Synoptic Overview: Water vapor and upper\nair analysis continues to show a rather messy/convoluted \npattern with a blocking pattern across the CONUS. An upper level\nlow continues to slowly move east across Indiana. A large ridge\nacross the Central Plains was also slowly moving east. The 12z \nILX sounding showed a decent amount of saturation in the low \nlevels but the column then dries out above 700mb. The upper low \nand moisture continues to allow for scattered to broken cumulus \nclouds around 2-4kft. Earlier this morning there were even a few\nmPING reports of drizzle given some weak lift and lack of cloud\nice. A few breaks in the clouds have allowed for temps to reach\nthe mid/upper 60s to around 70 early this afternoon. \n\nThrough Friday: Latest HREF/REFS guidance continues to favor\nmore clouds versus sun over the next few days as that low \npressure will be slow to slide east and additional energy moves \nin from the west. Other than a very rogue area of drizzle or \nsprinkles, most locations will remain dry. Have generally \ntrended closer to the consensus of high res models which keeps \nhighs a little lower than the NBM with most locations reaching \nthe low 70s each afternoon. The northeast flow should keep dews \nand therefore overnight lows in the 50s.\n\nLow Weekend Rain Chances: With the upper low moving east of the\narea Friday, additional energy looks to slide up and over the\nridge across Missouri during the weekend. With high pressure \nremaining over the Great Lakes, drier/stable air will prevail \nover Illinois which will inhibit much precip from making it very\nfar east into the state. Ensemble cluster analysis generally \nsuggests that the higher rain chances will also struggle to make\nit into the western tier or two of counties where a 15-30% \nchance of rain exists Saturday. Clouds on Saturday should keep \ntemps a little lower than previous days with some areas \nremaining in the upper 60s. Confidence is medium to high that \nmost locations will remain dry this weekend.\n\nHigher Rain Chances Around Next Tuesday/Wednesday: In between \nthe weekend system and early next week there will be little if \nany rain chances with gradually increasing temperatures. Ensembles\nare coming into agreement on an amplified trough moving into \nthe region by Tuesday/Wednesday of next week. NBM PoPs are \nalready in the 50-60% range and is also supported by all of the \nensemble clusters. As far as significant hazards go, the \nEnsemble Situational Awareness Table is not showing anything \nanomalous at this time and the area is not outlooked in any\nhazard/threat areas.",
